WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.380
Scientists have named about
1,424,000 living animal species.

2
00:00:06.430 --> 00:00:09.430
About 1,000,000 of them are insects.

3
00:00:09.480 --> 00:00:13.130
Every chordate named, including
all the mammals and birds,

4
00:00:13.180 --> 00:00:16.960
adds up to 64,788.

5
00:00:17.010 --> 00:00:20.120
And insects were the first animals to fly.

6
00:00:20.170 --> 00:00:24.200
So what about the insect body
plan made all this possible?

7
00:00:24.250 --> 00:00:28.170
In this mission, you'll take
apart an insect and a spider:

8
00:00:28.220 --> 00:00:31.630
their body regions, their
limbs and their joints.

9
00:00:31.680 --> 00:00:36.610
Then you'll set a bird beside an insect,
and find the feature that truly separates

10
00:00:36.660 --> 00:00:37.400
them.

11
00:00:37.450 --> 00:00:43.150
Your mission: explain what about the insect
body plan made so many species possible.
